# Permuto .gitignore
#
# Build output is never committed here. That is a rule with a gate behind it, not a
# preference: this repo used to carry its build/ tree in git (130 of its 169 tracked
# files were CMake output), which means a clone could not be trusted to build from
# source and the gate's own `tree` stage failed on it. The 2026-09-20 commit stopped
# tracking build/ and wired that stage into tools/ci.sh; the reason is in INCIDENTS.md.
# If build/ ever comes back as a tracked path, `tools/ci.sh tree` fails.

# --- build output (the gate builds in build/, build-asan/, build-tsan/) ---
build/
build-*/
out/

# --- the gate's own footprint (tools/ci.sh) ---
.ci-logs/
.ci.env

# --- object files and libraries ---
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe

# --- CMake droppings ---
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json
CMakeUserPresets.json

# --- editor / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- coverage ---
*.gcov
*.gcda
*.gcno
coverage/
